    "reading": {
        "body": "Adobe reported $23.8 billion in annual revenue as of November 2025 and operates four commercial-use AI products across image, video, and audio generation, all trained on commercially safe data.\n\nThe company has moved AI from research into production across its core creative suite. Adobe Express AI and Adobe Firefly handle image generation. Premiere Pro AI extends this to video with generative tools for content extension and color matching. Adobe Podcast AI covers audio enhancement. Each product emphasizes commercial safety in training, a positioning that reflects Adobe's customer base of professional and enterprise users who require legal clarity on training data provenance.\n\nThis portfolio reveals how AI embeds into existing software infrastructure rather than replacing it. Adobe does not appear to offer foundation models or standalone inference services. Its AI features integrate into licensed design and video tools that already consume power and compute resources. For data center operators, this means AI workloads added to products customers already use, not new categories of demand.\n\nThe data does not cover compute spend, energy consumption, model size, or Adobe's infrastructure footprint. It does not reveal whether Adobe trains models in-house or relies on third parties. California legal exposure registers at 175 instances, but no specific disputes are documented here.",
